# {{project.title}}

{{project.description}}.

A new axiz capability, built like the framework modules:

| Module | Layer | Contents |
|---|---|---|
| `{{project.name}}` | 1 | Plain Java API and implementation (no Spring) |
| `{{project.name}}-spring-boot-autoconfigure` | 2 | `{{platform.autoConfigurationClass}}` and `{{platform.propertiesClass}}` (`{{platform.prefix}}.*`) |
| `{{project.name}}-spring-boot-starter` | 2 | The dependency services add |

Rules: layer 1 never depends on Spring; the auto-configuration depends only on its own library
(and the foundation starter if needed); every bean is `@ConditionalOnMissingBean`; properties are an
immutable record with defaults; tests use `ApplicationContextRunner`. A capability that enters the
framework arrives through an RFC and with its use case in the demo.

`./mvnw verify` builds the three modules; `develop` publishes SNAPSHOTs and release tags publish
the release to Nexus. `version.txt` and `.release-please-manifest.json` hold the last released version (`0.0.0`:
nothing released yet); the pom holds the next one (`0.1.0-SNAPSHOT`). From `0.0.0` a `feat:` commit
makes the first release `0.1.0`.
